  "author": "Aster Clinical contributors",
  "description": "Clinician-selected possible NSTEMI or unstable angina; serial testing and risk assessment belong in emergency care.\nDRAFT; GUIDELINE-INFORMED, NOT AN ASTER CLINICAL PRESCRIPTION OR AN INDIVIDUAL MEDICAL ORDER. Requires clinician review. Independently written with references: 2025 ACC/AHA ACS Guideline https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacc.2024.11.009 ; 2025 Australian ACS Guideline https://www.heartfoundation.org.au/for-professionals/acs-guideline . No author/publisher endorsement.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "type": "investigations.add",
      "items": [
        {
          "manual_name": "12-lead ECG"
        },
        {
          "manual_name": "High-sensitivity cardiac troponin (I or T; local assay)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "advice.add_lines",
      "lines": [
        "Possible non-ST-elevation acute coronary syndrome requires urgent hospital assessment.",
        "One normal ECG or a negative early troponin test does not reliably exclude a heart attack.",
        "The emergency team will decide on repeat testing, monitoring, and further care.",
        "Arrange ambulance transport; do not drive yourself."
      ]
    }
  ]
